    "message": {
     "content": "### 1. Is this a good offer?\n\n**Yes, financially this is a strong initial offer for an L6 PM, but it has noticeable weak spots.**\n\nTo evaluate it accurately, you have to factor in Google\u2019s standard front-loaded vesting schedule for initial equity grants (typically **33% / 33% / 22% / 12%** over 4 years):\n\n| Component | Current (Meta IC6) | Google Offer (Year 1 & 2) | Google Offer (4-Yr Avg) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $235,000 | $235,000 |\n| **Target Bonus** | ~$36,000 (15%) | $47,000 (20%) | $47,000 |\n| **Equity (RSUs)**| ~$250,000 | **$356,400** (33% of $1.08M) | **$270,000** ($1.08M / 4) |\n| **Sign-on Bonus**| \u2014 | $0 | $0 |\n| **Total Target Comp** | **~$526,000** | **~$638,400** | **~$552,000** |\n\n#### Key Takeaways:\n* **The Pros:** Because Google front-loads new-hire grants, your Year 1 and Year 2 compensation would be **~$638,400/yr**\u2014an immediate **~$112,000/yr jump** over Meta. $1.08M in equity is at the upper-middle of the Google L6 PM band.\n* **The Cons:** \n  * **Base salary is a pay cut** ($235k vs. your current $240k), despite the posted band topping out at $271k.\n  * **$0 sign-on bonus** leaves money on the table, especially when you are walking away from unvested Meta RSUs and mid-cycle bonus accruals.\n  * **The \"Year 3\u20134 Cliff\":** In Year 3 ($237.6k vest) and Year 4 ($129.6k vest), equity drops significantly. While Google refreshers stack (typically 25% vesting per year), they depend on performance ratings and Alphabet stock trajectory.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Should you accept, negotiate, or walk away?\n\n**Negotiate.** \n\nYou are in a position of maximum leverage:\n1. **You weren\u2019t looking:** You have high job security and satisfaction at Meta.\n2. **They sought you out:** Google spent recruiting resources to interview and select you.\n3. **They gave a low base / zero sign-on starting point:** Tech recruiters rarely open with their best and final offer on non-equity cash components.\n\nAt big tech companies, polite, well-reasoned counteroffers almost never result in an offer being rescinded\u2014they simply say \u201cyes,\u201d \u201cno,\u201d or meet in the middle.\n\n---\n\n### 3. What to negotiate and exact numbers to ask for\n\nFocus your counteroffer on three components: **Base Salary**, **Sign-On Bonus**, and **Equity**.\n\n#### A. Base Salary: Ask for $255,000 \u2013 $260,000\n* **Why:** You currently make $240k base. Google's disclosed band goes up to $271k. It is reasonable to expect an increase in guaranteed base cash when switching companies.\n\n#### B. Sign-on Bonus: Ask for $75,000 \u2013 $100,000\n* **Why:** This is Google\u2019s most flexible lever to bridge compensation gaps without warping their standard leveling bands. Use your upcoming unvested Meta shares ($200k over the next 12 months) and any forfeited bonus timing as your rationale.\n\n#### C. Equity (GSUs): Ask for $1,200,000 ($300k/yr average)\n* **Why:** Rounding up from $1.08M to $1.2M is a reasonable bump that provides extra insurance against the Year 3/4 drop-off.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Counter-Script / Email Framework\n\n> *\"Thank you again for putting this offer together. I\u2019ve enjoyed meeting the team and am genuinely excited about the impact of this role.*\n>\n> *I wasn't actively looking to leave Meta, where I'm well-supported, valued, and tracking comfortably at ~$526k total compensation. To take on the transition risk and walk away from upcoming vesting equity and bonus cycles, I\u2019d like to see if we can close the gap on a few areas:*\n>\n> 1. * **Base Salary:** Given my current base of $240k and the posted range up to $271k, I'd like to target **$255,000**.\n> 2. * **Sign-on Bonus:** To help offset the unvested Meta equity and forfeited bonus timing I\u2019d be leaving behind over the next 12 months, I'm requesting a **$75,000 sign-on bonus**.\n> 3. * **Equity:** I\u2019d like to explore increasing the initial equity grant to **$1,200,000** over 4 years.\n>\n> *If we can get the package closer to these numbers, I\u2019d be thrilled to sign and focus fully on joining the team.\"*",
