    "message": {
     "content": "**Yes, you should accept this offer.** \n\nGetting a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus** on top of matching your base salary ($240k) and keeping the $1.08M equity grant puts this offer firmly in the **top tier (95th+ percentile) for a Google L6 Product Manager**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Financial Breakdown: An Extraordinary Year 1\n\n| Component | Current (Meta IC6) | Google Revised (Year 1) | Google (4-Yr Baseline Avg)* |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 |\n| **Target Bonus** | ~$36,000 (15%) | $48,000 (20%) | $48,000 |\n| **Equity (RSUs)** | ~$250,000 | **$356,400** (33% of $1.08M) | **$270,000** ($1.08M / 4) |\n| **Sign-on Bonus** | $0 | **$200,000** | $50,000/yr |\n| **Total Comp** | **~$526,000** | **~$844,400** | **~$608,000/yr** |\n\n*\\*Note: The 4-year baseline average does not even include annual equity refreshers or stock appreciation.*\n\n#### Key Financial Highlights:\n* **Year 1:** You are looking at roughly **~$844,000** in total target compensation (or ~$744k/yr if the sign-on is split into two annual installments of $100k). That is an immediate **+$318,000 (+60%) cash and equity surge** over your current Meta package.\n* **Offsetting your lost unvested Meta equity:** You walked away from $200k in unvested Meta RSUs over the next 12 months, and Google literally handed you **$200,000 in upfront cash** *while* simultaneously vesting **$356,400 in Alphabet stock** in Year 1. You come out substantially ahead.\n* **4-Year Baseline:** Even without a single refresher grant, your floor over the next 4 years is **~$608,000/year**, a $328,000 total increase over staying at Meta's baseline.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Strategic and Career Considerations\n\nSince compensation is resolved and overwhelmingly positive, the decision comes down to the environment:\n\n1. **Product Culture Differences:**\n   * **Meta (IC6):** Highly execution-heavy, fast-moving, bottom-up, and metrics/impact-obsessed with rigorous, stack-ranked semi-annual reviews.\n   * **Google (L6):** More consensus-driven, cross-functional stakeholder management, slightly longer product cycles, but generally more sustainable work-life balance and psychological safety.\n2. **Career Optionality & Resume Value:**\n   * Having both **Meta IC6** and **Google L6** PM titles on your resume establishes you as an elite top-tier PM for future Director/VP or startup CPO opportunities.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Final Checklist Before Signing\n\nBefore you verbally accept and sign the paperwork, clarify two administrative details with the recruiter:\n\n1. **Sign-On Payment Schedule & Clawback:**\n   * Ask whether the $200,000 is paid as a single lump sum in your first 30 days or split across Year 1 and Year 2 ($100k / $100k).\n   * Confirm the clawback duration (standard is prorated over 12 or 24 months).\n2. **Start Date & Meta Equity Timing:**\n   * Time your Google start date so you don't miss an imminent Meta quarterly vest date (e.g., February 15 / May 15 / August 15 / November 15) by just a couple of weeks if you are close to one.\n\n**Conclusion:** Google met your walk-away threshold with hard cash. Sign the offer and celebrate a massive win.",
